WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:16.400
Messier 83 or M83, also known as the Southern Pinwheel Galaxy and NGC 5236, is a barred spiral galaxy approximately 15 million light-years away from Earth in the constellation borders of Hydra and Centaurus.

00:16.877 --> 00:24.002
Nicolas-Louis de Lacaille discovered M83 on 17 February 1752 at the Cape of Good Hope.

00:24.569 --> 00:30.135
Charles Messier added it to his catalogue of nebulous objects in March 1781.
